==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 13.33~33.33 seconds<sup>400f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Kang Roo]]s spawn, delay 20~46.67 seconds<sup>600f~1,400f</sup>.
**4 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 26.67~53.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,600f</sup>.
**4 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.67 seconds<sup>2f~20f</sup>.
**1 [[Shadow Boxer K]] spawns.
**1 [[Shadow Boxer K]] spawns.
**1 [[Shadow Boxer K]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Here's an important fact if you're hesitant to try this stage: If your cheaper cats ([[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and below) can finish [[Sweet XP (Veteran)]] with little to no help from [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]], you can most likely beat this stage too with the same cats (including heavy attackers) as long as there are enough [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Cooldown Cats]] and [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Cat Eastwoods]] when Director Kurosawah spawns. So expect this to be similar to the veteran stage, besides there being a Director Kurosawah.

